course: dictionary
lesson: 3752
title: Fluorescent: bright colours that seem to glow
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Fluorescent means very bright, and it seems to glow, especially in colours like bright yellow, orange or green. Look at the words around it. «In daylight, bright fluorescent colours help you stand out.» Standing out means being easy to see, so fluorescent must mean very bright.
explain: «Fluorescent colours show up best in daylight and do little at night.» The clues tell you these colours need daylight or other light to be seen well. Try the swap test: put "very bright and easy to see" in place of fluorescent and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A fluorescent colour is a bright colour, but a fluorescent light is a long glass tube light, like the ones in many classrooms. Read the whole sentence to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Fluorescent means very bright and seeming to glow, especially colours like bright yellow, orange or green.
fact: Fluorescent things give out bright light when energy such as ultraviolet light shines on them.
fact: A fluorescent light is a long glass tube light, and many school rooms have them.
fact: «Fluorescent jacket» and «fluorescent armband» help drivers see walkers and cyclists, especially in poor light.
fact: «Reflective material» is different: it shines back light from headlights at night, which is why it helps when fluorescent colours do little.
exercise: «In daylight, bright fluorescent colours help you stand out.» What does fluorescent mean here? | *Very bright and easy to see | Cold and wet | Very heavy and slow to move | Quiet and soft to touch
exercise: «Fluorescent colours show up best in daylight and do little at night.» Why do fluorescent colours do little at night? | They are too heavy to lift | *They need daylight or other light to show up | They are made of glass | They never glow at all
exercise: Ella sees «a fluorescent light» in her classroom. What is a fluorescent light? | Sunlight on a hill | *A long glass tube light | A torch with batteries | A candle in a jar
test: A driver must see a walker at dusk. Which item helps most? | *Fluorescent armband | Plain black coat | Wooden walking stick | Glass jar
test: Which item shines back light from headlights at night? | *Reflective material | Summer rain | Fluorescent colours | Daylight
exam: «Fluorescent colours glow brightly in daylight.» Which meaning fits best? | Very cold and wet | Very dull and grey | Very old and worn | *Very bright and seeming to glow
